Task 1: Set Up Authentication Policies for Workloads
Subtask 1.1: Deploy Sample Applications
First, we'll deploy sample applications that will be used throughout this lab.

Create a new project namespace:
oc new-project bookinfo-auth
Label the namespace for Istio injection:
oc label namespace bookinfo-auth istio-injection=enabled
Deploy the Bookinfo sample application:
oc apply -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/istio/istio/release-1.19/samples/bookinfo/platform/kube/bookinfo.yaml -n bookinfo-auth
Verify the deployment:
oc get pods -n bookinfo-auth
Wait until all pods are in Running status with 2/2 containers ready (indicating both the application container and Istio sidecar are running).

Subtask 1.2: Configure Mutual TLS (mTLS) Authentication
Create a PeerAuthentication policy to enforce strict mTLS:
cat <<EOF | oc apply -f -
apiVersion: security.istio.io/v1beta1
kind: PeerAuthentication
metadata:
  name: default
  namespace: bookinfo-auth
spec:
  mtls:
    mode: STRICT
EOF
Verify the PeerAuthentication policy:
oc get peerauthentication -n bookinfo-auth
Create a mesh-wide PeerAuthentication policy:
cat <<EOF | oc apply -f -
apiVersion: security.istio.io/v1beta1
kind: PeerAuthentication
metadata:
  name: default
  namespace: istio-system
spec:
  mtls:
    mode: STRICT
EOF
Subtask 1.3: Configure Request Authentication with JWT
Create a RequestAuthentication policy for JWT validation:
cat <<EOF | oc apply -f -
apiVersion: security.istio.io/v1beta1
kind: RequestAuthentication
metadata:
  name: jwt-auth
  namespace: bookinfo-auth
spec:
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: productpage
  jwtRules:
  - issuer: "testing@secure.istio.io"
    jwksUri: "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/istio/istio/release-1.19/security/tools/jwt/samples/jwks.json"
EOF
Verify the RequestAuthentication policy:
oc get requestauthentication -n bookinfo-auth
Task 2: Configure Service-to-Service Authorization Policies
Subtask 2.1: Create Basic Authorization Policies
Create a deny-all authorization policy as a baseline:
cat <<EOF | oc apply -f -
apiVersion: security.istio.io/v1beta1
kind: AuthorizationPolicy
metadata:
  name: deny-all
  namespace: bookinfo-auth
spec:
  {}
EOF
Verify the policy is created:
oc get authorizationpolicy -n bookinfo-auth
Test the deny-all policy by attempting to access the application:
# Get the productpage service
oc get svc productpage -n bookinfo-auth

# Try to access the service (this should fail)
oc exec -n bookinfo-auth deployment/ratings-v1 -c ratings -- curl -s productpage:9080/productpage
Subtask 2.2: Configure Specific Service Authorization
Create an authorization policy to allow productpage to access other services:
cat <<EOF | oc apply -f -
apiVersion: security.istio.io/v1beta1
kind: AuthorizationPolicy
metadata:
  name: productpage-viewer
  namespace: bookinfo-auth
spec:
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: productpage
  rules:
  - from:
    - source:
        principals: ["cluster.local/ns/bookinfo-auth/sa/bookinfo-productpage"]
  - to:
    - operation:
        methods: ["GET"]
EOF
Create authorization policy for details service:
cat <<EOF | oc apply -f -
apiVersion: security.istio.io/v1beta1
kind: AuthorizationPolicy
metadata:
  name: details-viewer
  namespace: bookinfo-auth
spec:
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: details
  rules:
  - from:
    - source:
        principals: ["cluster.local/ns/bookinfo-auth/sa/bookinfo-productpage"]
    to:
    - operation:
        methods: ["GET"]
EOF
Create authorization policy for reviews service:
cat <<EOF | oc apply -f -
