Subtask 2.3: Configure JWT-based Authorization
Create an authorization policy that requires valid JWT tokens:
cat <<EOF | oc apply -f -
apiVersion: security.istio.io/v1beta1
kind: AuthorizationPolicy
metadata:
  name: require-jwt
  namespace: bookinfo-auth
spec:
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: productpage
  rules:
  - from:
    - source:
        requestPrincipals: ["testing@secure.istio.io/testing@secure.istio.io"]
EOF
Create a more granular JWT-based policy with custom claims:
cat <<EOF | oc apply -f -
apiVersion: security.istio.io/v1beta1
kind: AuthorizationPolicy
metadata:
  name: jwt-claims-auth
  namespace: bookinfo-auth
spec:
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: productpage
  rules:
  - when:
    - key: request.auth.claims[iss]
      values: ["testing@secure.istio.io"]
    - key: request.auth.claims[sub]
      values: ["testing@secure.istio.io"]
EOF
Task 3: Test Authentication and Authorization Flow
Subtask 3.1: Test mTLS Authentication
Verify mTLS is working by checking certificate information:
# Check if mTLS is enabled
istioctl authn tls-check productpage.bookinfo-auth.svc.cluster.local
Test service-to-service communication with mTLS:
# Execute from within the mesh
oc exec -n bookinfo-auth deployment/productpage-v1 -c productpage -- curl -s details:9080/details/0
Verify mTLS certificates are being used:
# Check proxy configuration
istioctl proxy-config cluster productpage-v1-<pod-suffix>.bookinfo-auth --fqdn details.bookinfo-auth.svc.cluster.local
Subtask 3.2: Test Authorization Policies
Test that unauthorized access is blocked:
# This should fail due to authorization policies
oc exec -n bookinfo-auth deployment/details-v1 -c details -- curl -s productpage:9080/productpage
Test authorized access:
# This should succeed
oc exec -n bookinfo-auth deployment/productpage-v1 -c productpage -- curl -s details:9080/details/0
Verify authorization policy logs:
# Check access logs for authorization decisions
oc logs -n bookinfo-auth deployment/productpage-v1 -c istio-proxy | grep -i "rbac"
Subtask 3.3: Test JWT Authentication
Generate a valid JWT token for testing:
# Create a script to generate JWT token
cat <<EOF > generate-jwt.py
#!/usr/bin/env python3
import json
import jwt
import time

# JWT payload
payload = {
    'iss': 'testing@secure.istio.io',
    'sub': 'testing@secure.istio.io',
    'aud': 'productpage',
    'exp': int(time.time()) + 3600,  # 1 hour from now
    'iat': int(time.time())
}

# Generate token (using 'secret' as key for demo purposes)
token = jwt.encode(payload, 'secret', algorithm='HS256')
print(token)
EOF

python3 generate-jwt.py > jwt-token.txt
Test access without JWT token:
# Remove the require-jwt policy temporarily to test
oc delete authorizationpolicy require-jwt -n bookinfo-auth

# Create a test pod to make external requests
oc run test-client --image=curlimages/curl:latest --rm -it --restart=Never -n bookinfo-auth -- sh

# Inside the test pod, try to access without JWT
curl -s productpage:9080/productpage
Test access with valid JWT token:
# Re-apply the JWT requirement policy
oc apply -f - <<EOF
apiVersion: security.istio.io/v1beta1
kind: AuthorizationPolicy
metadata:
  name: require-jwt
  namespace: bookinfo-auth
spec:
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: productpage
  rules:
  - from:
    - source:
        requestPrincipals: ["testing@secure.istio.io/testing@secure.istio.io"]
EOF

# Test with JWT token
TOKEN=$(cat jwt-token.txt)
oc exec -n bookinfo-auth deployment/productpage-v1 -c productpage -- curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" -s productpage:9080/productpage
Subtask 3.4: Monitor and Debug Authentication/Authorization
Check Istio proxy configuration:
# View authentication policies
istioctl proxy-config listeners productpage-v1-<pod-suffix>.bookinfo-auth --port 9080 -o json

# View authorization policies
istioctl proxy-config rbac productpage-v1-<pod-suffix>.bookinfo-auth
Enable access logging for debugging:
cat <<EOF | oc apply -f -
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: istio
  namespace: istio-system
data:
  mesh: |
    accessLogFile: /dev/stdout
    defaultConfig:
      proxyStatsMatcher:
        inclusionRegexps:
        - ".*circuit_breakers.*"
        - ".*upstream_rq_retry.*"
        - ".*_cx_.*"
EOF
Restart pods to apply logging configuration:
oc rollout restart deployment/productpage-v1 -n bookinfo-auth
oc rollout restart deployment/details-v1 -n bookinfo-auth
oc rollout restart deployment/reviews-v1 -n bookinfo-auth
oc rollout restart deployment/ratings-v1 -n bookinfo-auth
Monitor access logs:
# Watch access logs in real-time
oc logs -f deployment/productpage-v1 -c istio-proxy -n bookinfo-auth
Subtask 3.5: Test Policy Combinations
Create a complex authorization policy combining multiple conditions:
cat <<EOF | oc apply -f -
apiVersion: security.istio.io/v1beta1
kind: AuthorizationPolicy
metadata:
  name: complex-auth
  namespace: bookinfo-auth
spec:
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: productpage
  rules:
  - from:
    - source:
        principals: ["cluster.local/ns/bookinfo-auth/sa/bookinfo-productpage"]
    to:
    - operation:
        methods: ["GET", "POST"]
        paths: ["/productpage*"]
    when:
    - key: source.ip
      notValues: ["192.168.1.100"]
  - from:
    - source:
        requestPrincipals: ["testing@secure.istio.io/testing@secure.istio.io"]
    to:
    - operation:
        methods: ["GET"]
    when:
    - key: request.headers[user-agent]
      values: ["*curl*"]
EOF
Test the complex policy:
# Test with different user agents and methods
oc exec -n bookinfo-auth deployment/productpage-v1 -c productpage -- curl -H "User-Agent: curl/7.68.0" -s productpage:9080/productpage

# Test with different HTTP methods
oc exec -n bookinfo-auth deployment/productpage-v1 -c productpage -- curl -X POST -s productpage:9080/productpage
Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: mTLS Connection Failures
Symptoms: Services cannot communicate, connection refused errors

Solution:

# Check if all pods have Istio sidecars
oc get pods -n bookinfo-auth -o jsonpath='{range .items[*]}{.metadata.name}{"\t"}{.spec.containers[*].name}{"\n"}{end}'

# Verify PeerAuthentication policies
oc get peerauthentication -A

# Check proxy status
istioctl proxy-status
Issue 2: Authorization Policy Not Working
Symptoms: Requests are allowed when they should be denied

Solution:

# Verify policy syntax and selectors
oc describe authorizationpolicy -n bookinfo-auth

# Check if policies are applied to correct workloads
istioctl proxy-config rbac <pod-name>.<namespace>

# Verify service account names
oc get sa -n bookinfo-auth
Issue 3: JWT Validation Failures
Symptoms: Valid JWT tokens are being rejected

Solution:

# Verify RequestAuthentication configuration
oc describe requestauthentication -n bookinfo-auth

# Check if JWKS endpoint is accessible
curl -s https://raw.githubusercontent.com/istio/istio/release-1.19/security/tools/jwt/samples/jwks.json

# Validate JWT token format and claims
echo $TOKEN | base64 -d
