Why This Matters: Authentication and authorization are critical security components in microservices architectures. By implementing these policies in OpenShift Service Mesh, you ensure that:

Only authenticated services can communicate with each other
Access is granted based on the principle of least privilege
End-user requests are properly validated and authorized
Security policies are consistently enforced across all services
Compliance requirements are met through proper access controls
These skills are essential for building secure, production-ready microservices applications and are directly applicable to the Red Hat Certified Specialist in Building Resilient Microservices exam. The hands-on experience gained in this lab provides practical knowledge of implementing zero-trust security models in cloud-native environments.

